<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia reduces Tapis price for November.</title>
<headline>Malaysia reduces Tapis price for November.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian state oil company Petronas has lowered its November-lifting Tapis crude oil price to $25.06 per barrel, down 64 cents from $25.70 in October, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>For December, Petronas has set a premium of 60 cents per barrel for term crude oil sales, down from 75 cents in November.  </p>
<p>Current fixed differentials against Tapis for other Malaysian grades Labuan and Miri are unchanged, with Labuan 10 cents above Tapis, Miri 10 cents below Tapis and Bintulu 30 cents below Tapis.</p>
<p>The price of November Dulang crude was set at $24.10 per barrel, down 59 cents from 24.69 per barrel for October.</p>
